--TEST--
`Core\Bytes::at` reads an octet of an upload as a plain `uint`, and `Core\Bytes::join` takes `array<tainted bytes>` and gives `tainted bytes`, which a plain `bytes` variable does not take: rule:security/taint-propagation
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Bytes::at
// covers: Core\Bytes::join
final class Upload
{
    public static function check(tainted bytes $upload, array<tainted bytes> $parts): void
    {
        uint $first = Core\Bytes::at($upload, 0);
        tainted bytes $kept = Core\Bytes::join($parts, "-" as bytes);
        bytes $plain = Core\Bytes::join($parts);
    }
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `bytes`, found `tainted bytes`
   --> case.nvs:%d:%d
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
